<section id="A9" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix I </span>Experimental Results under Other Prompt Generation Ways</h2>

<div id="A9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To validate the robustness of AI-generated text across different prompts, we also conducted experiments under two other prompt generation ways:</p>
<ul id="A9.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A9.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A9.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">topical prompts (e.g. generating texts based on argument, news title, story topic);</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A9.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A9.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">specified prompts (e.g. specified source information like BBC news or Reddit posts).</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A9.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A9.T13" title="In Appendix I Experimental Results under Other Prompt Generation Ways ‣ MoSEs : Uncertainty-Aware AI-Generated Text Detection via Mixture of Stylistics Experts with Conditional Thresholds" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a> demonstrates that MoSEs consistently achieve optimal performance, aligning with the findings from continuation prompts.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A9.T13" class="ltx_table">
